<p>Australian authorities have charged former Special Air Service soldier Ben Roberts-Smith, once celebrated as Australia’s most decorated living soldier, with five war crime counts linked to the alleged killings of five unarmed Afghans during deployments between 2009 and 2012. Court documents cited across the reports say the charges include two counts of war crime murder and three counts of aiding or abetting murder. Police said the alleged victims were unarmed, under Australian military control, and not taking part in hostilities at the time. Police arrested Roberts-Smith on Tuesday, and he appeared in court on Wednesday. The court adjourned the case to June after his lawyer did not seek bail, leaving him in custody in Sydney. He has consistently denied wrongdoing. The prosecution follows years of investigations into alleged misconduct by Australian special forces in Afghanistan.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OW7VEIlIANujq5R8yc3SLVsA1FHRlpQQzLutAmdZOW9t5b8xJ2CJCM6qY4euTMl5AQlZ08XuZa5Zw90K9MbPydnYgNUWsnaQmL0gfr9KjjX6' alt='Ben Roberts-Smith arrives at the Federal Court of Australia in Sydney, May 18, 2022.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Defamation fallout: Roberts-Smith’s public standing shifted sharply after newspaper reports in 2018 accused him of unlawfully killing Afghan civilians. He later lost a high-profile defamation case against Nine newspapers.</li><li>Second charged: The Associated Press, as quoted by The Week, said Roberts-Smith is only the second Australian veteran of the Afghanistan war to face a war crimes charge.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Andrew Hastie: The Liberal MP, who served alongside Roberts-Smith in Afghanistan and later gave evidence in his defamation case, said Roberts-Smith is entitled to the presumption of innocence while stressing that nobody is above the law. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/09/ben-roberts-smith-presumption-innocence-andrew-law-hastie-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>BBC legal scholars: Scholars cited by the BBC said the case is extraordinary by international standards because countries rarely put one of their most decorated soldiers on trial over alleged wartime killings. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/czjwp1vjn9lo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>World Socialist Web Site: WSWS said the case raises broader questions about the role of Australian governments and military command in overseeing and concealing alleged abuses during the Afghanistan war. (<a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/04/09/myys-a09.html'>WSWS</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/04/09/myys-a09.html'>Australian special forces soldier Ben Roberts-Smith charged with war crimes against Afghan civilians</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/08/nx-s1-5776855/once-seen-as-a-war-hero-australian-ex-soldier-will-stand-trial-for-alleged-war-crimes'>Once seen as a war hero, Australian ex-soldier will stand trial for alleged war crimes</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/czjwp1vjn9lo'>He&#x27;s Australia&#x27;s most decorated soldier. Now he&#x27;s at the centre of a historic war crimes case</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/09/ben-roberts-smith-presumption-innocence-andrew-law-hastie-ntwnfb'>Ben Roberts-Smith entitled to presumption of innocence but ‘none of us are above the law’, Andrew Hastie says</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/australia-charges-former-war-hero-crimes'>Australia charges former war hero with war crimes</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1990019/australian-soldier-charged-with-war-crimes-to-stay-in-jail'>Australian soldier charged with war crimes to stay in jail</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>